hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"198","Bundar and Muhammad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Abu Asim narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Salam bin Junada narrated to us, Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan. Ahmad ibn Mani’ and Muhammad ibn Rafi’ narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qais al-Awdi, on the authority of Huzail bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “performed ablution and wiped over his socks.” And the sandals.” Abu Bakr said: There is no report from Abu Asim about sandals. Rather, he said: he wiped over the socks. Ibn Rafi’ said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace “He urinated, performed ablution, and wiped over his socks and sandals.”"
